Scenario: B (sophie.davis@demo.com) selects Pharmacy (id 3), logs out -> guest
session re-mints (NEARS-570). Fresh guest (id 749) checked before any selection,
then guest taps "Continue as Guest" (re-mints again to guest id 750 on this app's
first real guest-cart touch) and lands on a store.

run-as pref read right after B's Pharmacy selection + logout (guest id 749, no
selection made yet):
  flutter.cacheModuleId::u:sophie.davis@demo.com = {"id":3,"module_name":"Pharmacy",...}
  flutter.cacheModuleId::u:michael.brown@demo.com = {"id":1,"module_name":"Grocery & Food",...}
  (no cacheModuleId::g:749 key -- guest inherited NOTHING)

After guest 750 lands on a pharmacy store (auto single-module-select feature,
unrelated to this ticket) and its own selection is persisted:
  flutter.cacheModuleId::g:750 = {"id":3,"module_name":"Pharmacy",...}
  (same VALUE as sophie's own key by coincidence -- but a DIFFERENT KEY, no shared
  storage; sophie's u: key and the guest's g: key never collided)

CONFIRMS: a fresh guest never inherits a departed guest's or a prior logged-in
user's cached sector.

Minor unrelated finding logged separately (see
bug-clearshareddata-header-rebuild-order.log): during the ~1s window of the
NEARS-570 guest re-mint itself, 2 requests (the un-awaited cm-firebase-token
invalidation POST + the guestLogin() call) carry the departing user's STALE
moduleId header, because AuthRepository.clearSharedData()'s own updateHeader()
rebuild (line ~367, clearing the header) runs AFTER guestLogin() (line ~357),
not before. auth_repository.dart's clearSharedData() is untouched by this
ticket's diff -- pre-existing, out of scope, filed as regression_bugs.
